00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:09.440
clotting potential side effect.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:10.960
Prescription hydroquinone cream. The

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:12.960
stronger formulations from a

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:14.880
dermatologist are the most effective

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:17.200
option. My derm also prescribed a

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:19.200
combination cream that's tininoan plus

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:20.720
hydroquinone which is the synergistic

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:22.400
pairing that I mentioned earlier. There

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:25.280
was also another cream I got which was

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:27.600
hydroquinone with kic acid and this is a

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:29.520
compounded formula. Lastly, glutathione

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:31.919
injections. I wasn't prescribed this and

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:33.600
I didn't try this but most spots do

00:21:31.919 --> 00:21:35.840
offer it and my dermatologist offers

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:37.360
that as well. So ask your doctor if this

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:39.200
is appropriate for you. Other

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:40.880
modalities. Now, let's talk about

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:42.960
everything beyond the products and the

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:44.960
prescriptions that I did to speed up my

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:46.960
healing. The first one is hypobaric

00:21:44.960 --> 00:21:48.880
oxygen therapy. So, the place that

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:50.880
botched my laser also offered this to

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:53.039
me. If you have access to it and you're

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:55.440
healing from any kind of injury at all,

00:21:53.039 --> 00:21:57.360
it is a very powerful healing tool. I

00:21:55.440 --> 00:21:59.600
will say though, after a couple weeks,

00:21:57.360 --> 00:22:02.080
you do get diminishing returns and it's

00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:04.320
also very expensive. So, it's most

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:06.640
useful in the early acute phase of

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:08.720
healing. LED light therapy. This one is

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:10.400
a bit more nuanced and I need to be more

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:11.760
careful and specific about this because

00:22:10.400 --> 00:22:14.240
I've been getting conflicting

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:16.480
inflammation. My dermatologist actually

00:22:14.240 --> 00:22:18.400
recommended that I avoid red light for

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:20.000
pigmentation which I was surprised by

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:22.159
because I love red light therapy. But

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:24.480
her reasoning was specifically that heat

00:22:22.159 --> 00:22:26.000
of any kind can worsen pigmentation and

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:28.159
I believe she meant this specifically

00:22:26.000 --> 00:22:30.400
for my Asian skin which is more prone to

00:22:28.159 --> 00:22:32.400
hyperpigmentation. It may be different

00:22:30.400 --> 00:22:34.480
for you, but generally speaking,

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:37.200
powerful red light and especially

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:38.880
infrared light generates heat and then

00:22:37.200 --> 00:22:40.320
heat increases inflammation, which is

00:22:38.880 --> 00:22:42.000
the opposite of what you want when

00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:44.960
you're trying to calm overactive

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:47.120
melanosides. We want our skin to remain

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:50.000
cool. Personally, I think that the

00:22:47.120 --> 00:22:52.000
gentler light LED face masks are okay.

00:22:50.000 --> 00:22:53.840
And because it's closer to your skin, it

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:56.240
really doesn't generate as much heat at

00:22:53.840 --> 00:22:58.559
all compared to the big expensive

00:22:56.240 --> 00:23:01.919
panels. So, I strongly believe in this

00:22:58.559 --> 00:23:03.840
case it's actually better to do DIY at

00:23:01.919 --> 00:23:05.520
home treatments compared to going to a

00:23:03.840 --> 00:23:07.360
salon because the panels that they use

00:23:05.520 --> 00:23:10.240
at the salons, at the med spas and

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:12.159
recovery places are incredibly strong

00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:14.240
and you don't actually want that in this

00:23:12.159 --> 00:23:16.000
case. Infrared light is great for muscle

00:23:14.240 --> 00:23:17.120
pain. It's great for reaching deeper

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:19.520
layers of your skin. It promotes

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:21.440
cellular regeneration, but the strong

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:22.480
ones does generate a lot of heat. It

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:24.720
might be too intense while you're

00:23:22.480 --> 00:23:26.720
actively treating pigmentation. What is

00:23:24.720 --> 00:23:28.400
recommended across the board, and I also

00:23:26.720 --> 00:23:30.960
found research backing this up, is

00:23:28.400 --> 00:23:34.240
yellow light and green light. A 2025

00:23:30.960 --> 00:23:36.159
study found that 505 NM green LED light

00:23:34.240 --> 00:23:38.400
inhibited melanin synthesis. There's

00:23:36.159 --> 00:23:40.480
another 2021 study in the International

00:23:38.400 --> 00:23:42.720
Journal of Molecular Sciences, and that

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:44.159
study found combined green and yellow

00:23:42.720 --> 00:23:46.400
light treatments synergistically

00:23:44.159 --> 00:23:48.799
together reduce inflammation and melanin

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:50.320
production in UV damaged skin cells much

00:23:48.799 --> 00:23:52.480
faster than if you were to use them

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:54.880
separately. So, that's what I actually

00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:57.760
do. I use both yellow and green light

00:23:54.880 --> 00:24:00.080
settings on my LED mask. And then I also

00:23:57.760 --> 00:24:02.960
have a green light panel, so I layer

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:05.520
that on top of the LED face mask. I have

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:07.679
seen a visible result from doing this

00:24:05.520 --> 00:24:09.280
combination alone compared to just using

00:24:07.679 --> 00:24:11.039
the yellow light and then the green

00:24:09.280 --> 00:24:13.120
light as well. Remember, I'm trying to

00:24:11.039 --> 00:24:15.039
speedrun this thing and heal as quickly

00:24:13.120 --> 00:24:16.559
as possible. So, I'm absolutely throwing

00:24:15.039 --> 00:24:18.400
everything I can in the wall. So,

